1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,817
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,983 --> 00:00:06,637
In this lesson, we will keep deployment
activity and cost evidence together.

3
00:00:06,809 --> 00:00:11,757
Extended mutual aid work needs
clear personnel, apparatus, dates,

4
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:15,552
and cost records that can be
reviewed after demobilization.

5
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:19,439
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:19,439 --> 00:00:21,558
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:22,365 --> 00:00:27,288
A strike team deployment is recorded
with its personnel, apparatus, and dates.

8
00:00:27,514 --> 00:00:31,002
Keep deployment records and
cost documentation together

9
00:00:31,003 --> 00:00:32,636
for review and reimbursement.

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,772
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

11
00:00:36,774 --> 00:00:39,220
scenarios, not default settings.

12
00:00:40,025 --> 00:00:41,469
Deployment finance.

13
00:00:41,677 --> 00:00:44,427
Deployment records and deployment finance.

14
00:00:44,634 --> 00:00:48,299
Record your next deployment with
its personnel and apparatus.

15
00:00:49,102 --> 00:00:50,111
New deployment.

16
00:00:50,338 --> 00:00:54,347
Start a deployment record, useful
when your members deploy to

17
00:00:54,348 --> 00:00:56,556
incidents outside your jurisdiction.

18
00:00:57,349 --> 00:00:59,293
Deployment from external order.

19
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:03,601
Create a deployment from a mutual
aid resource order, useful when

20
00:01:03,602 --> 00:01:07,082
your members deploy to incidents
outside your jurisdiction.

21
00:01:07,875 --> 00:01:11,265
Resource orders describe
requested resources and the fills

22
00:01:11,265 --> 00:01:13,133
departments offer or accept.

23
00:01:13,321 --> 00:01:16,800
Review ordering settings and
participating departments.

24
00:01:17,018 --> 00:01:21,484
Create a fictional request, offer
a fill, and review acceptance.

25
00:01:21,669 --> 00:01:27,169
Reconcile requested quantities, accepted
fills, and the remaining resource need.

26
00:01:27,383 --> 00:01:30,389
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

27
00:01:30,389 --> 00:01:32,048
recording the live workflow.

28
00:01:32,857 --> 00:01:36,898
An external order records the
department fills and their mobilization,

29
00:01:37,073 --> 00:01:39,484
release, and actual return home.

30
00:01:39,693 --> 00:01:44,714
Enter an approved sample external order,
link its deployment, record the fill

31
00:01:44,714 --> 00:01:47,209
transitions, and complete closeout.

32
00:01:47,387 --> 00:01:49,645
Review dates and resource identity.

33
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:53,810
This workspace records manual
entry and artifact snapshots.

34
00:01:53,979 --> 00:01:56,453
It is not an external ordering connector.

35
00:01:56,651 --> 00:01:59,658
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

36
00:01:59,658 --> 00:02:01,324
recording the live workflow.

37
00:02:02,136 --> 00:02:06,830
Read-only deployment reports bring
time entries, supporting artifacts,

38
00:02:07,005 --> 00:02:08,877
and export outputs together.

39
00:02:09,069 --> 00:02:12,877
Open a recorded demo deployment
and review its time report,

40
00:02:13,082 --> 00:02:15,503
summary, and available exports.

41
00:02:15,683 --> 00:02:20,732
Reconcile each time entry with the roster
and recorded dates before finance review.

42
00:02:20,954 --> 00:02:23,958
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

43
00:02:23,959 --> 00:02:25,618
recording the live workflow.

44
00:02:26,457 --> 00:02:29,343
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

45
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:34,209
Step one: create a deployment or
start from an external resource order.

46
00:02:34,435 --> 00:02:40,319
Step two: identify the assigned personnel,
apparatus, and operational dates.

47
00:02:40,561 --> 00:02:45,909
Step three: record deployment activity
and finance documentation for review.

48
00:02:46,719 --> 00:02:48,349
Now verify the result.

49
00:02:48,552 --> 00:02:52,784
Reconcile the deployment resources
and dates with supporting records.

50
00:02:52,985 --> 00:02:57,553
Review any daily time and cost
documentation required by the workflow.

51
00:02:57,744 --> 00:03:01,922
A common problem to watch for,
deployment finance is separate from

52
00:03:01,923 --> 00:03:03,822
the business operations add-on.

53
00:03:04,039 --> 00:03:07,221
A prepared record does not
guarantee reimbursement.

54
00:03:07,995 --> 00:03:09,819
Your practice task is simple.

55
00:03:09,971 --> 00:03:13,845
Record a two-day demo strike team
deployment, then reconcile the

56
00:03:13,846 --> 00:03:17,452
participating people and units
with the supporting documents.

57
00:03:17,646 --> 00:03:22,158
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

58
00:03:22,295 --> 00:03:26,220
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
